  "as_of": "2018-11-29",
  "sentences": [
   "This bill would stop religious schools from excluding students because of their sexuality, gender identity or variation in sex characteristics.",
   "It would remove exemptions in the Sex Discrimination Act 1984 that currently let those schools turn away pupils on those grounds.",
   "The bill does not change indirect discrimination rules, so faith-based schools could still set reasonable conditions based on their religion's teachings."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "Removes exemptions for religious schools that allow discrimination against students based on sexual orientation, gender identity or intersex status.",
   "Leaves indirect discrimination provisions unchanged.",
   "Does not address discrimination against staff at religious schools."
  ],
  "affected": "Students attending religious schools, and religious schools themselves.",
